# Minime shared libretro cores manifest
#
# Single source of truth for every RetroArch core that Minime builds once and
# ships in BOTH MinUI and Allium. buildcores.sh consumes this file.
#
# Format (pipe-separated, '#' comments):
#   core       - recipe/core name (clone dir). Artifact is <core>_libretro.so
#                unless core_so overrides it.
#   repo       - git URL to clone.
#   hash       - pinned commit. Empty = float at the repo's default branch.
#                The update-cores bot bumps hashes for autobump=1 entries only.
#   buildpath  - directory of the Makefile, relative to the CLONE root.
#                Empty = the clone root itself.
#   makefile   - Makefile filename to pass via `make -f`. Empty = Makefile.
#   flags      - extra make variables passed verbatim to the build.
#   patch      - patch file under patches/ applied before building. Empty = none.
#   platform   - make `platform=` value. Empty = minime.
#   core_so    - output .so basename. Empty = <core>_libretro.so.
#   optional   - 1 = skip+warn on build failure (CI stays green), 0 = fail.
#   autobump   - 1 = update-cores bot may bump hash, 0 = keep pinned forever.
#
# The 13 recipes below are carried over verbatim from the old MinUI build
# (workspace/minime/cores/makefile); handy + mednafen_wswan cover the Atari
# Lynx / WonderSwan Roms systems; yabasanshiro (Saturn, WIP, pinned) and
# drastic (NDS, WIP; public wrapper only, proprietary core stays private).

